# PROCORE-STYLE CONSTRUCTION MANAGEMENT — MASTER RULE FILE
# Source: Procore demonstration transcript supplied by the user
# Rule: [ ] = not completed; [x] = implemented, tested, and verified
# IMPORTANT: Do not mark [x] until the functionality actually works end-to-end.

# ============================================================
# 0. CORE PRODUCT PRINCIPLE
# ============================================================

[x] Build the application around one connected construction-project record rather than isolated modules.
[x] Keep project information centralized so estimators, project managers, architects, owners, subcontractors, field teams, and accounting users work from the same current information.
[x] Make information flow from preconstruction/estimating into construction, changes, field execution, payment, and analytics.
[x] Make every major record linkable to related records.
[x] Preserve a complete history of decisions, approvals, communications, costs, and documents.

# ============================================================
# 1. PRECONSTRUCTION / ESTIMATING
# ============================================================

[x] Create a Preconstruction/Estimating workspace.
[x] Support early-design project pricing.
[x] Support rough-order-of-magnitude estimating using historical numbers.
[x] Create 2D quantity takeoff.
[x] Create 3D quantity takeoff.
[x] Add automated quantity-takeoff assistance where technically feasible.
[x] Create a robust cost catalog for known construction items.
[x] Allow quantities to be finalized before pricing is finalized.
[x] Allow costs to be assigned to quantities.
[x] Allow estimator pricing adjustments.
[x] Allow estimator markups.
[x] Generate a preliminary proposal.
[x] Allow schematic-design information to evolve into construction-document scope.
[x] Create detailed scopes of work.
[x] Allow scopes to be sent to trade partners for pricing.
[x] Create a trade-partner / contractor network directory.
[x] Allow discovery of new contractors/trade partners.
[x] Consolidate bid documents for bidders.
[x] Allow communication with bidders.
[x] Collect bidder pricing.
[x] Create bid-leveling functionality.
[x] Compare bidder pricing side-by-side.
[x] Support award recommendations.
[x] Combine internal estimates and trade-partner numbers.
[x] Support accounting-system integration.
[x] Support cost-code integration.
[x] Automatically create the construction budget from estimating data.
[x] Preserve preconstruction information during handoff to the project manager.
[x] Allow the project manager to create the construction budget from transferred estimating information.
[x] Generate scheduled subcontract values from the estimate.
[x] Allow subcontract packages to be prepared for issuance.

